{"groups":[{"members":["c1"],"primary":"c1","title":"Los Angeles Just Cause for Eviction Ordinance (JCO)","requirement":"Landlords of covered units not regulated by the RSO may terminate a tenancy only for a listed at-fault or no-fault just cause, and must pay relocation assistance for no-fault evictions. Landlords may not evict for non-payment unless the amount owed exceeds the Fair Market Rent for the unit's bedroom size, and must file all eviction notices with LAHD within 3 business days of service.","key_value":"Applies after 6 months of tenancy or expiry of the original lease, whichever comes first; relocation assistance required for no-fault evictions; no non-payment eviction unless rent owed exceeds FMR (effective 2023-03-27); eviction notices filed with LAHD within 3 business days of service","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"City of Los Angeles Just Cause for Eviction Ordinance (LAMC 165.00 et seq.)","coverage_conditions":"Most residential properties in the City of Los Angeles that are not regulated by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO), including buildings built after October 1, 1978 and a property with only one single-family dwelling. Applies once the tenant has lived in the unit at least six months or the original lease has expired, whichever comes first.","exemptions":"Transient hotels, licensed care facilities, fraternity or sorority houses, the owner's roommate, cooperatives under certain circumstances, some non-profit facilities for the homeless or short-term substance abuse treatment centers, and some properties owned by HACLA or the government. Units subject to the RSO are regulated by the RSO instead.","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance - legal reasons for eviction","requirement":"RSO tenancies may be ended only for listed at-fault or no-fault reasons. For a no-fault eviction the landlord must file a Landlord Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD, give written notice, and pay relocation assistance, and must file all termination notices with LAHD within 3 business days of service with the RSO notice attached.","key_value":"30-day and 60-day written notice for no-fault evictions (some require 120 days or up to a 1-year extension), with relocation assistance; termination notices filed with LAHD within 3 business days of service","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance, LAMC 151.09 (source also cites LAMC 151.09.C.9 and 165.05.B.5)","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (generally built on or before October 1, 1978, per the RSO coverage list).","exemptions":null,"conflict_note":null},{"members":["c3"],"primary":"c3","title":"Los Angeles RSO/JCO relocation assistance and Declaration of Intent to Evict for no-fault evictions","requirement":"For no-fault evictions from RSO or JCO units, the landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD before serving the termination notice and must file a copy of the notice with LAHD within 3 days of service. The landlord must pay relocation assistance per unit within 15 days of service of the notice, or place it in escrow within that period, in an amount set by tenant eligibility, length of tenancy and income.","key_value":"Chart A (July 1, 2026 to June 30, 2027): Eligible household $11,000 (under 3 years) or $14,400 (3+ years or low income); Qualified household $23,150 or $27,400; Mom & Pop $10,550 (eligible) or $21,250 (qualified); single-family dwelling owned by a natural person (JCO only) one month's rent. Amounts increase every July 1.","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"LAMC 151.09, 165.03, 165.06","coverage_conditions":"Units covered by the Los Angeles RSO or JCO. Qualified tenant: 62 or older, handicapped or disabled, or with one or more minor dependent children. The Mom and Pop reduced amount requires four or fewer units in the building, no use of the provision in the prior three years, an owner with no more than four units plus one single-family home in the City, and an eligible relative who owns no residential property in the City.","exemptions":"Relocation assistance is not required when evicting a resident manager to replace them with another resident manager (a Manager-Tenant may still be entitled), or when evicting due to hazardous conditions caused by a natural disaster not caused by the landlord's negligence. The landlord may offset accumulated rent against the payment, except where the termination is required by a governmental order to vacate.","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c4"],"primary":"c4","title":"Los Angeles Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO) - relocation for demolition of Protected Units","requirement":"When a Protected Unit is demolished for new construction, the landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict (JCO units) or a Notice of Intent to Withdraw (RSO units) with LAHD, serve written notice and file it with LAHD within 3 business days, and pay relocation at the higher of State Housing Crisis Act or City amounts. Tenants have a right to remain up to 6 months before construction starts, a right to return if demolition does not proceed, and in some cases a right of first refusal.","key_value":"Option 1 standardized payments (July 1, 2026 to June 30, 2027): Extremely Low Income $115,480; Very Low Income $96,750; Low Income $87,450; households above low income are paid under Chart A (RSO/JCO amounts). Penalties start at $250,000 per displaced unit.","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2025-02-11","end_date":null,"citation":"Los Angeles Ordinance Nos. 188481 and 188482 (Resident Protections Ordinance)","coverage_conditions":"Applies only to Protected Units demolished for new construction within 5 years after filing the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict. All RSO units are Protected Units. Protected Units also include units subject to affordability covenants or rent control within the past five years, units rented by lower or very low income households within the past five years, and units withdrawn under the Ellis Act within the past 10 years.","exemptions":"If the units to be demolished are not Protected Units or are not occupied by a lower income tenant, the regular RSO or JCO relocation rules apply.","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
